# Netlify redirects. Format: <from> <to> <status>
#
# Hotel slug changes. A hotel's slug is its URL segment, so when a property
# rebrands and we rename the slug, the old URL has to keep resolving — both for
# anything already indexed and for links out in the wild.

# Thompson Hollywood -> The Hollywood Grande, Autograph Collection (2025-07-29,
# Hyatt to Marriott). Renamed 2026-07-18.
/cities/los-angeles/thompson-hollywood/  /cities/los-angeles/hollywood-grande/  301

# Retired affiliate redirectors. /go/<provider>/<slug> was an interstitial that
# auto-forwarded to the Commission Junction click URL; removed 2026-08-30
# because an affiliate click may not pass through an auto-forwarding page of
# ours (ref. policy 5.1.1). The pages were noindex,nofollow and sitemap-excluded,
# so little should point here — but browser history and any stray shared link
# would otherwise 404. Sent home rather than on to CJ: forwarding these would
# recreate the exact hop that was removed.
/go/*  /  301
